/-!
# Finite coefficient subrings detect relative differentials

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tags 07P4, 07P5 and 07PH.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-power-series-polynomial-nonzero-differential)
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
universe u v w t

namespace KaehlerDifferential

/-- In a finite extension of the fraction field of a polynomial ring over power
series, a non-pth-power has a nonzero differential over a finite coefficient subring.
Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 07PH (`lemma-find-D`), paragraph
beginning with the finite extension of the polynomial ring, and Tags 07P4, 07P5.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-power-series-polynomial-nonzero-differential)

Proof: choose a p-basis (t_i) of k. For finite J let k_J be generated by k^p
and the basis elements outside J, and put C_J = k_J[[x_1^p,...,x_n^p]]
[y_1^p,...,y_m^p], transported to C through e. Tag 07P5 says C is finite
over each C_J; their fraction subfields K_J contain K^p, have intersection
K^p, and satisfy K_(J union J') contained in both K_J and K_J'.
In the finite extension M/K, the second assertion of Tag 07P4 gives that
the intersection of T_J = M^p K_J is M^p. These subfields contain M^p and
are directed downwards, since forming M^p K_J preserves inclusion. The
absolute differential of z over the prime field is nonzero by Tag 031W,
as z is not a pth-power. Apply the first assertion of Tag 07P4 to M and
the family T_J: it supplies J for which this differential has nonzero
image in the differentials over T_J. The image of C_J lies in T_J, so
the universal property gives a map from differentials over C_J to those
over T_J sending d z to d z. Hence the differential of z over C_J is nonzero.
Take A = C_J. This argument handles n = 0 or m = 0 as well: the corresponding
variables are simply absent; if k is perfect and both vanish, there is no
non-pth-power in the finite extension, so the hypothesis is impossible. -/
theorem exists_finite_subring_nonzero_differential
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]
    (k : Type t) [Field k] [CharP k p] (n m : ℕ)
    (C : Type u) [CommRing C] [IsDomain C]
    (e : C ≃+* MvPolynomial (Fin m) (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
    (K : Type v) [Field K] [Algebra C K] [IsFractionRing C K]
    (M : Type w) [Field M] [CharP M p] [Algebra C M]
    [Algebra K M] [IsScalarTower C K M] [FiniteDimensional K M]
    (z : M) (hz : ¬ ∃ x : M, x ^ p = z) :
    ∃ A : Subring C,
      letI : Algebra A M := ((algebraMap C M).comp A.subtype).toAlgebra
      Module.Finite A C ∧ D A M z ≠ 0 := by sorry

end KaehlerDifferential
